Track 3: Vance's Rooftop Gantry
- Story & Context: Years after the transit authority welded the doors shut, locals swear that Vance's Rooftop Gantry still picks up a hollow metallic hum echoing through the abandoned subway tunnels of the Midnight Crawler. The legend grew that the ghosts of the insomniac commuters had permanently magnetized the iron rails, leaving the tracks to autonomously loop the aggressive Rhodes chords and shattered jungle breaks every night at 3 AM. If you climb to the rooftop and press your ear to the copper exhaust pipes, you can hear the mechanical afterlife singing, "We left our teeth in the iron gears."
